d November 2 at 6:25PM MST until November 3 at 2:30PM MST by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall will continue along\nthe reaches of the San Juan River above Navajo Reservoir to near\nthe confluence with the Rio Blanco River.\n\n* WHERE...South Central Archuleta County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 230 PM MST Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is occurring. Numerous roads remain\nclosed due to flooding.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 620 PM MST, The river gauge on the San Juan at Pagosa Springs\nis reporting moderate to minor flooding continuing overnight with\nthis water working downstream to the reservoir.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nGato, Juanita and Pagosa Junction.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-03T14:30:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.296bbf99475527b7bc31e99b4aa69e7b0a30d2d6.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.296bbf99475527b7bc31e99b4aa69e7b0a30d2d6.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-11-02T23:47:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 022347 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 447 PM MST Mon Nov 2 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Rivers across southwest CO and southeast UT remain rain swollen due to runoff. The San Juan River at Pagosa Springs remains in major flood stage. - Light rain below 10000 feet will continue, with snow above. Winter weather highlights continue for the mounta","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-11-02T18:59:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... This is an automatically generated forecast with no discussion. The normal Fire Weather Forecast will resume in its entirety in the spring. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTE